cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, dataset, or harness, please cite the following technical report (V11 — Second Update, 100,000 synthetic test cases)."
type: software
title: "Kantesti AI Blood Test Benchmark — V11 (Second Update, 100,000 Synthetic Cases) and V12 November Update"
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered, rubric-based automated technical benchmark of the Kantesti
  blood-test interpretation engine on 100,000 synthetically generated test
  cases, tagged with 127 country labels and 75+ language labels to exercise
  multilingual output formatting. This is the Second Update of the V11
  Kantesti Blood Test Benchmark suite, extending the original V11 release
  (15 hand-constructed synthetic cases) to a larger synthetic cohort while
  keeping the V11 scoring rubric byte-identical. On this rubric the engine
  produced a composite score of approximately 0.998 (99.80%), a mean
  end-to-end response latency of 13.26 seconds, and zero hyperdiagnosis flags
  on the trap subset. These figures describe output conformance on generated
  inputs; they are not a clinical validation and not a measure of diagnostic
  accuracy. No real patient data or personal data of any kind is used. The
  repository also contains the V12 November Update (15 November 2026)
  results on four public medical benchmarks (MedQA, MedCalc-Bench, MedHallu,
  PubMedQA) with per-question raw answers. All results are vendor-run and
  have not been independently verified or peer-reviewed. The evaluation
  harness is released under the MIT licence.
